# MEASURED guest network-profile declaration (guest-io-integration).
#
# Sourced by the trusted supervisor (busybox sh KEY=VALUE only). These values
# are the VERIFIED upstream gvproxy v0.8.9 release in its UNCONFIGURED (no
# -config) NAT profile, which is the user-pinned transport for BOTH the Zed
# external-client path and the native Mini path (controller40 `network`
# decision; loop40-native-nat-repair3/net-helper/GUEST-IMAGE-PROFILE-HANDOFF.md).
# gvproxy's fixed profile (cmd/gvproxy/config.go, pkg/virtualnetwork/services.go)
# is subnet 192.168.127.0/24, gateway 192.168.127.1, and a resolver that binds
# ONLY to the gateway IP -- so DNS is 192.168.127.1, never a distinct 10.0.2.3.
# The static guest address 192.168.127.2 is valid for the v3 NIC MAC
# 02:00:00:00:00:15 (Mini) and the QEMU NIC MAC 5a:94:ef:e4:0c:ee (Zed) as a
# STATIC config: the DHCP static lease only constrains DHCP assignment, so a
# static .2 is permitted on any MAC (pkg/tap/ip_pool.go).
#
# NO egress/LAN-isolation claim is made by this file -- it only configures the
# interface the backend provides (the native backend owns the virtio-net device
# + NAT transport handoff; the Zed path uses QEMU -netdev stream to the gvproxy
# external-client socket). Changing these values changes the MEASURED image
# identity.
GUEST_IFACE=eth0
GUEST_IP_CIDR=192.168.127.2/24
GUEST_GW=192.168.127.1
GUEST_DNS=192.168.127.1
